IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spam-act`

-- Spam Control Act 2007 -- worked cases for Parts 1 to 3.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the
-- law. Nothing here has been checked against a decided case. The purpose is to
-- fix the answers so that a later change which moves one is caught.

§ `Fixtures`

-- A message with nothing unusual about it: sent to a real address, arrived,
-- commercial in purpose, and neither requested nor consented to.
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN AddressKind,
      `the purpose` IS A PrimaryPurpose,
      `requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Message
DECIDE `a message` `the kind` `the purpose` `requested` IS
    Message WITH
        `the kind of address it was sent to` IS `the kind`
        `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number` IS FALSE
        `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service` IS FALSE
        `the electronic address exists` IS TRUE
        `the message reached its intended destination` IS TRUE
        `the primary purpose` IS `the purpose`
        `the recipient requested to receive the message` IS `requested`
        `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message` IS FALSE
        `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient` IS FALSE
        `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request` IS FALSE

`a cold email advertising a product` MEANS
    `a message` `an email address` `to advertise or promote goods or services` FALSE

`a requested email advertising a product` MEANS
    `a message` `an email address` `to advertise or promote goods or services` TRUE

`a cold text advertising a product` MEANS
    `a message` `a mobile telephone number` `to advertise or promote goods or services` FALSE

`a cold message to a messaging app advertising a product` MEANS
    `a message` `an instant messaging account` `to advertise or promote goods or services` FALSE

`a cold email about nothing commercial` MEANS
    `a message` `an email address` `something the section does not name` FALSE

`a cold email offering to help a fraud` MEANS
    `a message` `an email address` `to assist a person by deception to dishonestly obtain property` FALSE

-- s 4(3): a voice call is not an electronic message however commercial it is.
`a cold sales telephone call` MEANS Message WITH
    `the kind of address it was sent to` IS `a mobile telephone number`
    `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number` IS FALSE
    `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service` IS TRUE
    `the electronic address exists` IS TRUE
    `the message reached its intended destination` IS TRUE
    `the primary purpose` IS `to advertise or promote goods or services`
    `the recipient requested to receive the message` IS FALSE
    `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message` IS FALSE
    `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient` IS FALSE
    `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request` IS FALSE

-- s 4(2): neither of these two facts is read by anything.
`a cold email to a dead address that never arrived` MEANS Message WITH
    `the kind of address it was sent to` IS `an email address`
    `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number` IS FALSE
    `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service` IS FALSE
    `the electronic address exists` IS FALSE
    `the message reached its intended destination` IS FALSE
    `the primary purpose` IS `to advertise or promote goods or services`
    `the recipient requested to receive the message` IS FALSE
    `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message` IS FALSE
    `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient` IS FALSE
    `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request` IS FALSE

-- s 5(2): the recipient put the address on a website, and that is the only
-- ground on which consent is said to rest.
`an email to an address scraped from the recipient's own website` MEANS Message WITH
    `the kind of address it was sent to` IS `an email address`
    `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number` IS FALSE
    `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service` IS FALSE
    `the electronic address exists` IS TRUE
    `the message reached its intended destination` IS TRUE
    `the primary purpose` IS `to advertise or promote goods or services`
    `the recipient requested to receive the message` IS TRUE
    `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message` IS FALSE
    `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient` IS TRUE
    `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request` IS FALSE

-- s 5(3): a subscriber who unsubscribed, and the sender kept going.
`an email to a subscriber who unsubscribed a fortnight ago` MEANS Message WITH
    `the kind of address it was sent to` IS `an email address`
    `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number` IS FALSE
    `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service` IS FALSE
    `the electronic address exists` IS TRUE
    `the message reached its intended destination` IS TRUE
    `the primary purpose` IS `to advertise or promote goods or services`
    `the recipient requested to receive the message` IS TRUE
    `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message` IS TRUE
    `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient` IS FALSE
    `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request` IS TRUE

-- s 4A: an account on a messaging service whose handle is the user's mobile
-- number. The number is how the account is addressed in practice, and s 4A says
-- the message is not sent to the number.
`a message to a messaging account named by the recipient's mobile number` MEANS Message WITH
    `the kind of address it was sent to` IS `an instant messaging account`
    `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number` IS TRUE
    `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service` IS FALSE
    `the electronic address exists` IS TRUE
    `the message reached its intended destination` IS TRUE
    `the primary purpose` IS `to advertise or promote goods or services`
    `the recipient requested to receive the message` IS FALSE
    `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message` IS FALSE
    `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient` IS FALSE
    `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request` IS FALSE

§§ `Who sent it`

`the person who pressed send` MEANS PersonsPart WITH
    `sent the message` IS TRUE
    `caused the message to be sent` IS FALSE
    `authorised the sending of the message` IS FALSE
    `knowingly allowed their product to be advertised or promoted by a sender` IS FALSE
    `took reasonable steps to stop the sending` IS FALSE

-- s 3(4): the advertiser who knew and did nothing.
`the advertiser who knew and did nothing` MEANS PersonsPart WITH
    `sent the message` IS FALSE
    `caused the message to be sent` IS FALSE
    `authorised the sending of the message` IS FALSE
    `knowingly allowed their product to be advertised or promoted by a sender` IS TRUE
    `took reasonable steps to stop the sending` IS FALSE

-- s 3(5): the same advertiser, who tried to stop it. The steps need not have
-- worked.
`the advertiser who tried to stop it` MEANS PersonsPart WITH
    `sent the message` IS FALSE
    `caused the message to be sent` IS FALSE
    `authorised the sending of the message` IS FALSE
    `knowingly allowed their product to be advertised or promoted by a sender` IS TRUE
    `took reasonable steps to stop the sending` IS TRUE

`a stranger to the mailing` MEANS PersonsPart WITH
    `sent the message` IS FALSE
    `caused the message to be sent` IS FALSE
    `authorised the sending of the message` IS FALSE
    `knowingly allowed their product to be advertised or promoted by a sender` IS FALSE
    `took reasonable steps to stop the sending` IS FALSE

§§ `Volumes`

GIVEN `in a day` IS A NUMBER, `in a month` IS A NUMBER, `in a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A SendingVolume
DECIDE `a volume of` `in a day` `in a month` `in a year` IS
    SendingVolume WITH
        `messages of similar subject matter sent during a 24-hour period` IS `in a day`
        `messages of similar subject matter sent during a 30-day period` IS `in a month`
        `messages of similar subject matter sent during a one-year period` IS `in a year`

`exactly 100 in a day and nothing more` MEANS `a volume of` 100 100 100
`101 in a day` MEANS `a volume of` 101 101 101
`50 a day, every day for a month` MEANS `a volume of` 50 1500 18000
`a single careful mailing of 90` MEANS `a volume of` 90 90 90
`90 a day on 11 days of the year` MEANS `a volume of` 90 990 990
`exactly 1,000 in a month` MEANS `a volume of` 90 1000 1000
`exactly 10,000 in a year` MEANS `a volume of` 90 990 10000
`10,001 in a year` MEANS `a volume of` 90 990 10001

§§ `A compliant mailing, and the ways to spoil it`

`a facility that meets every requirement by email` MEANS UnsubscribeFacility WITH
    `contains an address or number for submitting an unsubscribe request` IS TRUE
    `contains a statement to the effect that it may be so used` IS TRUE
    `the address provided is an email address` IS TRUE
    `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request` IS FALSE
    `the number provided also accepts a multimedia request at the recipient's option` IS FALSE
    `the statement is presented in a clear and conspicuous manner` IS TRUE
    `the statement is presented in English or in English among other languages` IS TRUE
    `valid and capable of receiving the request and similar requests for at least 30 days` IS TRUE
    `legitimately obtained` IS TRUE
    `using it costs no more than the usual cost of that kind of address or number` IS TRUE
    `no further unsolicited commercial message was sent after 10 business days from the request` IS TRUE

-- The same facility, but the return address is a postal address. Compliant under
-- para 2(1), which allows a postal address, and non-compliant under para 2(2),
-- which requires an email address where the message arrived by email.
`a facility offering only a postal address` MEANS UnsubscribeFacility WITH
    `contains an address or number for submitting an unsubscribe request` IS TRUE
    `contains a statement to the effect that it may be so used` IS TRUE
    `the address provided is an email address` IS FALSE
    `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request` IS FALSE
    `the number provided also accepts a multimedia request at the recipient's option` IS FALSE
    `the statement is presented in a clear and conspicuous manner` IS TRUE
    `the statement is presented in English or in English among other languages` IS TRUE
    `valid and capable of receiving the request and similar requests for at least 30 days` IS TRUE
    `legitimately obtained` IS TRUE
    `using it costs no more than the usual cost of that kind of address or number` IS TRUE
    `no further unsolicited commercial message was sent after 10 business days from the request` IS TRUE

-- para 2(4)(b): the statement is there, clear and conspicuous, in Mandarin only.
`a facility whose statement is not in English` MEANS UnsubscribeFacility WITH
    `contains an address or number for submitting an unsubscribe request` IS TRUE
    `contains a statement to the effect that it may be so used` IS TRUE
    `the address provided is an email address` IS TRUE
    `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request` IS FALSE
    `the number provided also accepts a multimedia request at the recipient's option` IS FALSE
    `the statement is presented in a clear and conspicuous manner` IS TRUE
    `the statement is presented in English or in English among other languages` IS FALSE
    `valid and capable of receiving the request and similar requests for at least 30 days` IS TRUE
    `legitimately obtained` IS TRUE
    `using it costs no more than the usual cost of that kind of address or number` IS TRUE
    `no further unsolicited commercial message was sent after 10 business days from the request` IS TRUE

-- para 2(5)(a): the address worked on the day the mailing went out and was shut
-- down a week later.
`a facility whose address was closed after a week` MEANS UnsubscribeFacility WITH
    `contains an address or number for submitting an unsubscribe request` IS TRUE
    `contains a statement to the effect that it may be so used` IS TRUE
    `the address provided is an email address` IS TRUE
    `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request` IS FALSE
    `the number provided also accepts a multimedia request at the recipient's option` IS FALSE
    `the statement is presented in a clear and conspicuous manner` IS TRUE
    `the statement is presented in English or in English among other languages` IS TRUE
    `valid and capable of receiving the request and similar requests for at least 30 days` IS FALSE
    `legitimately obtained` IS TRUE
    `using it costs no more than the usual cost of that kind of address or number` IS TRUE
    `no further unsolicited commercial message was sent after 10 business days from the request` IS TRUE

-- para 2(3)(b): received by multimedia messaging, and the return number takes
-- texts only. The recipient's option is not given.
`a facility giving a text-only number` MEANS UnsubscribeFacility WITH
    `contains an address or number for submitting an unsubscribe request` IS TRUE
    `contains a statement to the effect that it may be so used` IS TRUE
    `the address provided is an email address` IS FALSE
    `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request` IS TRUE
    `the number provided also accepts a multimedia request at the recipient's option` IS FALSE
    `the statement is presented in a clear and conspicuous manner` IS TRUE
    `the statement is presented in English or in English among other languages` IS TRUE
    `valid and capable of receiving the request and similar requests for at least 30 days` IS TRUE
    `legitimately obtained` IS TRUE
    `using it costs no more than the usual cost of that kind of address or number` IS TRUE
    `no further unsolicited commercial message was sent after 10 business days from the request` IS TRUE

`labelling that meets every requirement` MEANS Labelling WITH
    `there is a subject field` IS TRUE
    `the title in the subject field is not false or misleading` IS TRUE
    `the letters ADV appear with a space before the title in the subject field` IS TRUE
    `the letters ADV appear in the words first appearing in the message` IS FALSE
    `the header information is not false or misleading` IS TRUE
    `an accurate and functional address by which the sender can be readily contacted is given` IS TRUE

`labelling with no ADV` MEANS Labelling WITH
    `there is a subject field` IS TRUE
    `the title in the subject field is not false or misleading` IS TRUE
    `the letters ADV appear with a space before the title in the subject field` IS FALSE
    `the letters ADV appear in the words first appearing in the message` IS FALSE
    `the header information is not false or misleading` IS TRUE
    `an accurate and functional address by which the sender can be readily contacted is given` IS TRUE

-- A text message has no subject field, so para 3(1)(a) falls away and the ADV
-- must lead the message instead.
`labelling with no subject field and ADV first` MEANS Labelling WITH
    `there is a subject field` IS FALSE
    `the title in the subject field is not false or misleading` IS FALSE
    `the letters ADV appear with a space before the title in the subject field` IS FALSE
    `the letters ADV appear in the words first appearing in the message` IS TRUE
    `the header information is not false or misleading` IS TRUE
    `an accurate and functional address by which the sender can be readily contacted is given` IS TRUE

`labelling with no subject field and no ADV anywhere` MEANS Labelling WITH
    `there is a subject field` IS FALSE
    `the title in the subject field is not false or misleading` IS FALSE
    `the letters ADV appear with a space before the title in the subject field` IS FALSE
    `the letters ADV appear in the words first appearing in the message` IS FALSE
    `the header information is not false or misleading` IS TRUE
    `an accurate and functional address by which the sender can be readily contacted is given` IS TRUE

`labelling with a forged header` MEANS Labelling WITH
    `there is a subject field` IS TRUE
    `the title in the subject field is not false or misleading` IS TRUE
    `the letters ADV appear with a space before the title in the subject field` IS TRUE
    `the letters ADV appear in the words first appearing in the message` IS FALSE
    `the header information is not false or misleading` IS FALSE
    `an accurate and functional address by which the sender can be readily contacted is given` IS TRUE

§§ `Singapore link`

`no connection with Singapore at all` MEANS SingaporeLink WITH
    `the message originates in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is sent` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an entity formed or recognised under the law of Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an entity with an office or place of business in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the device used to access the message is located in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the recipient is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS FALSE
    `the recipient is an entity carrying on business in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS FALSE
    `the message could not be delivered and would likely have been accessed on a device in Singapore` IS FALSE

-- A foreign sender, a foreign server, and a recipient who happened to open it
-- on a phone in Singapore. Limb (c) alone.
`opened on a phone in Singapore and nothing else` MEANS SingaporeLink WITH
    `the message originates in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is sent` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an entity formed or recognised under the law of Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an entity with an office or place of business in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the device used to access the message is located in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the recipient is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS FALSE
    `the recipient is an entity carrying on business in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS FALSE
    `the message could not be delivered and would likely have been accessed on a device in Singapore` IS FALSE

-- Limb (e) alone: the address was dead, so nobody opened anything anywhere.
`undeliverable, but would have been opened in Singapore` MEANS SingaporeLink WITH
    `the message originates in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is sent` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an entity formed or recognised under the law of Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the sender is an entity with an office or place of business in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the device used to access the message is located in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the recipient is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS FALSE
    `the recipient is an entity carrying on business in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS FALSE
    `the message could not be delivered and would likely have been accessed on a device in Singapore` IS TRUE

§§ `First Schedule`

`not authorised by anyone` MEANS Authorisation WITH
    `the sending is authorised by the Government or a statutory body` IS FALSE
    `on the occurrence of a public emergency` IS FALSE
    `in the public interest` IS FALSE
    `in the interests of public security or national defence` IS FALSE

`a statutory body's emergency broadcast` MEANS Authorisation WITH
    `the sending is authorised by the Government or a statutory body` IS TRUE
    `on the occurrence of a public emergency` IS TRUE
    `in the public interest` IS FALSE
    `in the interests of public security or national defence` IS FALSE

-- The public-interest limb on its own: the only one of the three that no
-- certificate can settle.
`a statutory body's mailing said to be in the public interest` MEANS Authorisation WITH
    `the sending is authorised by the Government or a statutory body` IS TRUE
    `on the occurrence of a public emergency` IS FALSE
    `in the public interest` IS TRUE
    `in the interests of public security or national defence` IS FALSE

-- Authorised by nobody, but asserted to be in the public interest. The first
-- limb of the paragraph is not satisfied, so the exclusion fails.
`a private mailing said to be in the public interest` MEANS Authorisation WITH
    `the sending is authorised by the Government or a statutory body` IS FALSE
    `on the occurrence of a public emergency` IS FALSE
    `in the public interest` IS TRUE
    `in the interests of public security or national defence` IS FALSE

§ `Sections 3 to 5 -- what the message is`

#ASSERT `the message is an electronic message` `a cold email advertising a product`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is an electronic message` `a cold sales telephone call`

-- s 4(2): neither of these two facts changes anything.
#ASSERT `the message is an electronic message` `a cold email to a dead address that never arrived`
#ASSERT `the message is an unsolicited commercial electronic message` `a cold email to a dead address that never arrived`

#ASSERT `the message is a commercial electronic message` `a cold email advertising a product`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is a commercial electronic message` `a cold email about nothing commercial`
#ASSERT `the message is a commercial electronic message` `a cold email offering to help a fraud`

-- A voice call with a commercial purpose is not a commercial electronic
-- message, because it is not an electronic message.
#ASSERT NOT `the message is a commercial electronic message` `a cold sales telephone call`

#ASSERT `the message is unsolicited` `a cold email advertising a product`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is unsolicited` `a requested email advertising a product`

-- s 5(2): publishing your own address is not a request or a consent.
#ASSERT `the message is unsolicited` `an email to an address scraped from the recipient's own website`

-- s 5(3): consent given and then withdrawn. Eleven business days later the
-- message is unsolicited even though the recipient did once ask for it.
#ASSERT `an email to a subscriber who unsubscribed a fortnight ago`'s `the recipient requested to receive the message`
#ASSERT `the message is unsolicited` `an email to a subscriber who unsubscribed a fortnight ago`

#ASSERT `the message is an unsolicited commercial electronic message` `a cold email advertising a product`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is an unsolicited commercial electronic message` `a requested email advertising a product`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is an unsolicited commercial electronic message` `a cold email about nothing commercial`

-- s 3(2) reaches the twelve purposes unevenly: it covers (d) to (l) and not the
-- three deception limbs.
#ASSERT `section 3(2) makes existence and lawfulness irrelevant` `to advertise or promote goods or services`
#ASSERT `section 3(2) makes existence and lawfulness irrelevant` `to advertise or promote a provider of such an opportunity`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(2) makes existence and lawfulness irrelevant` `to assist a person by deception to dishonestly obtain property`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(2) makes existence and lawfulness irrelevant` `to assist a person to dishonestly obtain a gain`

§ `Sections 2, 3(4) and 3(5) -- who the sender is`

#ASSERT `the person is the sender of the message` `the person who pressed send`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is the sender of the message` `a stranger to the mailing`

-- The advertiser who knew and did nothing is a sender by deeming, and is liable
-- as one. The advertiser who tried to stop it is not -- and s 3(5) does not ask
-- whether the attempt worked.
#ASSERT `the person is deemed by section 3(4) to have authorised the sending` `the advertiser who knew and did nothing`
#ASSERT `the person is the sender of the message` `the advertiser who knew and did nothing`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is deemed by section 3(4) to have authorised the sending` `the advertiser who tried to stop it`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is the sender of the message` `the advertiser who tried to stop it`

§ `Section 4A -- the messaging account named by a mobile number`

-- The address the account is known by is a mobile number, and s 4A says the
-- message is not sent to that number. This is not a quibble: it decides whether
-- Part 2 applies.
#ASSERT `a message to a messaging account named by the recipient's mobile number`'s `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is sent to a mobile telephone number for the purposes of this Act` `a message to a messaging account named by the recipient's mobile number`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is sent to an email address for the purposes of this Act` `a message to a messaging account named by the recipient's mobile number`
#ASSERT `the message is sent to a mobile telephone number for the purposes of this Act` `a cold text advertising a product`
#ASSERT `the message is sent to an email address for the purposes of this Act` `a cold email advertising a product`

§ `Section 6 -- bulk`

-- "More than" 100, so 100 exactly is not bulk and 101 is.
#ASSERT NOT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `exactly 100 in a day and nothing more` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `101 in a day` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

-- The same at each of the other two thresholds.
#ASSERT NOT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `exactly 1,000 in a month` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT NOT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `exactly 10,000 in a year` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `10,001 in a year` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

-- 50 a day is comfortably inside limb (a) and is caught by limb (b) within the
-- month and by limb (c) within the year. A sender has to satisfy all three at
-- once to stay outside the Act, and the daily figure that does so depends on how
-- many days a year the sender mails.
#ASSERT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `50 a day, every day for a month` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT NOT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `a single careful mailing of 90` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT NOT `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` `90 a day on 11 days of the year` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

§ `Section 7 and the First Schedule -- whether the Act applies`

#ASSERT NOT `the message has a Singapore link` `no connection with Singapore at all`
#ASSERT `the message has a Singapore link` `opened on a phone in Singapore and nothing else`
#ASSERT `the message has a Singapore link` `undeliverable, but would have been opened in Singapore`

#ASSERT NOT `this Act applies to the message` `a cold email advertising a product` `no connection with Singapore at all` `not authorised by anyone`
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the message` `a cold email advertising a product` `opened on a phone in Singapore and nothing else` `not authorised by anyone`

-- The First Schedule exclusion needs the Government's or a statutory body's
-- authorisation AND one of the three grounds. Either alone is not enough.
#ASSERT `the message is excluded by the First Schedule` `a statutory body's emergency broadcast`
#ASSERT `the message is excluded by the First Schedule` `a statutory body's mailing said to be in the public interest`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is excluded by the First Schedule` `a private mailing said to be in the public interest`
#ASSERT NOT `the message is excluded by the First Schedule` `not authorised by anyone`

#ASSERT NOT `this Act applies to the message` `a cold email advertising a product` `opened on a phone in Singapore and nothing else` `a statutory body's emergency broadcast`

-- First Schedule para 2 gives a conclusive certificate for the emergency and the
-- security limbs. The widest ground, the public interest, has none.
#ASSERT `a ministerial certificate can settle the doubt` `a statutory body's emergency broadcast`
#ASSERT NOT `a ministerial certificate can settle the doubt` `a statutory body's mailing said to be in the public interest`

§ `Sections 8 and 9 -- the mobile telephone hole`

#ASSERT `Part 2 applies to the message` `a cold email advertising a product`

-- s 8(2). This is the finding: Part 2 does not reach a text message at all, so
-- generating mobile numbers by permutation and texting every one of them
-- contravenes nothing in Part 2.
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 applies to the message` `a cold text advertising a product`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 9` `a cold text advertising a product` `the person who pressed send` `through the use of a dictionary attack`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 9` `a cold text advertising a product` `the person who pressed send` `through the use of address-harvesting software`

-- The identical conduct against email addresses does contravene s 9.
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 9` `a cold email advertising a product` `the person who pressed send` `through the use of a dictionary attack`
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 9` `a cold email advertising a product` `the person who pressed send` `through the use of address-harvesting software`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 9` `a cold email advertising a product` `the person who pressed send` `otherwise`

-- s 8(1): Part 2 does not care whether the message was commercial or
-- unsolicited. A harvested list used for a message nobody would call spam still
-- contravenes s 9.
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 9` `a cold email about nothing commercial` `the person who pressed send` `through the use of address-harvesting software`
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 9` `a requested email advertising a product` `the person who pressed send` `through the use of address-harvesting software`

-- And s 4A closes part of the hole: the same blast delivered to messaging
-- accounts, even accounts named by mobile numbers, is inside Part 2.
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies to the message` `a message to a messaging account named by the recipient's mobile number`
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 9` `a message to a messaging account named by the recipient's mobile number` `the person who pressed send` `through the use of a dictionary attack`

-- A person who is not the sender does not contravene s 9 however the addresses
-- were got.
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 9` `a cold email advertising a product` `a stranger to the mailing` `through the use of a dictionary attack`

§ `The Second Schedule`

-- Paragraph 2 on a compliant email mailing, and on each of the five defects.
#ASSERT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility that meets every requirement by email` `by email` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility offering only a postal address` `by email` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility whose statement is not in English` `by email` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility whose address was closed after a week` `by email` FALSE

-- The postal-address-only facility satisfies para 2(1), which permits a postal
-- address, and fails para 2(2), which does not. Delivered at a messaging
-- account instead, where neither 2(2) nor 2(3) bites, the same facility
-- complies.
#ASSERT `the channel-specific requirement is met` `a facility offering only a postal address` `at an instant messaging account`
#ASSERT NOT `the channel-specific requirement is met` `a facility offering only a postal address` `by email`
#ASSERT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility offering only a postal address` `at an instant messaging account` FALSE

-- para 2(3)(b): a text-capable number is enough for a text, and not enough for a
-- multimedia message, which must give the recipient the choice.
#ASSERT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility giving a text-only number` `by text messaging to a mobile telephone number` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility giving a text-only number` `by multimedia messaging to a mobile telephone number` FALSE

-- para 2(9): a reasonable mistake of fact lifts sub-paragraphs (1) to (7)
-- entirely. Every defect above disappears.
#ASSERT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility offering only a postal address` `by email` TRUE
#ASSERT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility whose address was closed after a week` `by email` TRUE
#ASSERT `paragraph 2 is complied with` `a facility giving a text-only number` `by multimedia messaging to a mobile telephone number` TRUE

-- But para 2(8) is not in the list 2(9) lifts, so the duty of confidence over an
-- unsubscribe request survives a mistaken mailing.
#ASSERT `paragraph 2(8) is contravened` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 2(8) is contravened` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 2(8) is contravened` FALSE FALSE

-- Paragraph 3.
#ASSERT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling that meets every requirement` `by email` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling with no ADV` `by email` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling with a forged header` `by email` FALSE

-- 3(1)(a) and 3(1)(b) both depend on whether there is a subject field. In a text
-- message there is none, so the title requirement falls away and the <ADV> must
-- lead the words of the message.
#ASSERT `the subject-title requirement is met` `labelling with no subject field and ADV first`
#ASSERT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling with no subject field and ADV first` `by text messaging to a mobile telephone number` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling with no subject field and no ADV anywhere` `by text messaging to a mobile telephone number` FALSE

-- para 3(3): none of paragraph 3 applies to a message sent to an instant
-- messaging account. A forged header and no <ADV> at all comply.
#ASSERT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling with a forged header` `at an instant messaging account` FALSE
#ASSERT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling with no subject field and no ADV anywhere` `at an instant messaging account` FALSE

-- para 3(2): and a mistake lifts paragraph 3 on any channel.
#ASSERT `paragraph 3 is complied with` `labelling with a forged header` `by email` TRUE

§ `Section 11 -- the duty, and the gap between it and the Schedule`

`a compliant email blast of 5,000` MEANS BulkMailing WITH
    `the message` IS `a cold email advertising a product`
    `the volume` IS `a volume of` 5000 5000 5000
    `the facility` IS `a facility that meets every requirement by email`
    `the labelling` IS `labelling that meets every requirement`
    `how it was received` IS `by email`
    `sent by mistake` IS FALSE

`an unlabelled email blast of 5,000` MEANS BulkMailing WITH
    `the message` IS `a cold email advertising a product`
    `the volume` IS `a volume of` 5000 5000 5000
    `the facility` IS `a facility that meets every requirement by email`
    `the labelling` IS `labelling with no ADV`
    `how it was received` IS `by email`
    `sent by mistake` IS FALSE

-- The same defective mailing, 90 messages instead of 5,000.
`an unlabelled email mailing of 90` MEANS BulkMailing WITH
    `the message` IS `a cold email advertising a product`
    `the volume` IS `a volume of` 90 90 90
    `the facility` IS `a facility that meets every requirement by email`
    `the labelling` IS `labelling with no ADV`
    `how it was received` IS `by email`
    `sent by mistake` IS FALSE

-- A messaging-app blast with a forged header, no label, and a proper unsubscribe
-- facility.
`a messaging-app blast with a forged header` MEANS BulkMailing WITH
    `the message` IS `a cold message to a messaging app advertising a product`
    `the volume` IS `a volume of` 5000 5000 5000
    `the facility` IS `a facility offering only a postal address`
    `the labelling` IS `labelling with a forged header`
    `how it was received` IS `at an instant messaging account`
    `sent by mistake` IS FALSE

-- A blast to a list of people who all asked for it.
`a requested email blast of 5,000 with no label` MEANS BulkMailing WITH
    `the message` IS `a requested email advertising a product`
    `the volume` IS `a volume of` 5000 5000 5000
    `the facility` IS `a facility that meets every requirement by email`
    `the labelling` IS `labelling with no ADV`
    `how it was received` IS `by email`
    `sent by mistake` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `section 11 imposes the duty` `a compliant email blast of 5,000` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule requirements are met` `a compliant email blast of 5,000`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 11` `a compliant email blast of 5,000` `the person who pressed send` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule requirements are met` `an unlabelled email blast of 5,000`
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 11` `an unlabelled email blast of 5,000` `the person who pressed send` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

-- THE GAP. The Second Schedule says "every unsolicited commercial electronic
-- message must contain" the <ADV> label. s 11, the only section that gives the
-- Schedule force, binds only a person sending in bulk. So the mailing of 90 fails
-- the Schedule and contravenes nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule requirements are met` `an unlabelled email mailing of 90`
#ASSERT NOT `section 11 imposes the duty` `an unlabelled email mailing of 90` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 11` `an unlabelled email mailing of 90` `the person who pressed send` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

-- s 10: Part 3 applies only to unsolicited commercial messages, so a bulk
-- mailing to a list that asked for it needs no label and no unsubscribe link.
#ASSERT NOT `section 11 imposes the duty` `a requested email blast of 5,000 with no label` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 11` `a requested email blast of 5,000 with no label` `the person who pressed send` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

-- The messaging-app blast: paragraph 3 does not apply to it (3(3)) and the
-- postal-only unsubscribe address satisfies paragraph 2 on that channel. Five
-- thousand unsolicited commercial messages with forged headers, no label, and a
-- post-box for unsubscribing, and the Schedule is satisfied.
#ASSERT `section 11 imposes the duty` `a messaging-app blast with a forged header` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule requirements are met` `a messaging-app blast with a forged header`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 11` `a messaging-app blast with a forged header` `the person who pressed send` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`

-- And the deemed sender bears the s 11 duty as much as the person who pressed
-- send, while the advertiser who took steps does not.
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 11` `an unlabelled email blast of 5,000` `the advertiser who knew and did nothing` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 11` `an unlabelled email blast of 5,000` `the advertiser who tried to stop it` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 11` `an unlabelled email blast of 5,000` `a stranger to the mailing` `the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted`
